# wotr-book.service — was the scheduled task "WOTR book" (daily 02:00,
# ExecutionTimeLimit five hours).
#
# The book dispatcher: one chapter a night, while Isaac sleeps. build/book_next.py says
# what the book needs; if a chapter is due, Claude Code runs headless on the
# subscription and the book-chapter workflow does the real work under book/<slug>/;
# then what landed is committed. build/book_dispatch.sh does the work;
# wotr-book.timer says when. Isaac approves or rejects at breakfast.
#
# The five-hour limit is book_dispatch.sh's own `timeout 5h` around the Claude step (it
# mirrors the Windows task's ExecutionTimeLimit): when it fires mid-chapter, claude is
# killed, the script logs it, refreshes GATES.md and commits whatever landed.
# TimeoutStartSec below is only the backstop, and it is longer on purpose — the unit's
# clock starts before the pull and book_next.py, so an equal limit would have systemd
# kill the whole cgroup (script included) just before the script's timeout, and the
# chapter on disk would sit uncommitted with nothing in the log. WOTR_BOOK_OFF=1 in
# ~/.config/wotr/env is the off switch: the dispatcher writes nothing.
#
# ExecStartPre waits (up to two minutes) for DNS: with Persistent=true on the timer and
# linger on, a 02:00 the machine slept through runs at the next boot, when the user
# manager starts — before the network is up. Waits, never fails: the run goes ahead
# regardless and logs what it could not do.
#
# Logs: journalctl --user -u wotr-book, and the script's own build/book_dispatch.log.
# If an n8n workflow takes over the book, disable wotr-book.timer so it does not run
# twice (build/systemd_setup.sh prints the command).

[Unit]
Description=WOTR book: one chapter a night, gated

[Service]
Type=oneshot
WorkingDirectory=%h/wotr-rule-index
EnvironmentFile=-%h/.config/wotr/env
Environment=PYTHONIOENCODING=utf-8
ExecStartPre=/bin/bash -c 'for i in {1..24}; do getent hosts github.com >/dev/null 2>&1 && exit 0; sleep 5; done; exit 0'
ExecStart=/bin/bash %h/wotr-rule-index/build/book_dispatch.sh
TimeoutStartSec=5h30min
